Z||000003||ChadMan||11-12-1999||08:43 AM||||I wanted 3M TA3, so all the Dodge minivans and gold-package Camrys who won't relinquish the passing lane to faster traffic could look in their rear-view mirrors and see what's on my mind.  But Ohio DOT wouldn't let me have it!<P>Some of the cooler Fiero vanity plates I've seen include:<BR>BAD SIX<BR>FLYN LO<BR>LED INDY (on Pace Car, of course)<BR>XTINCT||||reg||10
Z||000004||fiero56||11-12-1999||09:36 AM||||There was a guy at the Columbus nationals this year. He had a re-body(can't remember which one it was, but it was sweet)and his plates said "TOO FAR".  I believe he was from Wiconsin. I'd have to go through my pile pf photos to refresh my memory.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-12-1999).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||deceler8||11-12-1999||11:33 AM||||Funny, those Ohio folks are tough...tried to get "WTA FUG" one year and they wouldn't let me have it.<P>I figured people would look at it and say..."W-T-A-F-U-G...wta fug does that stand for ?"<P>Also thought I'd make a statement by getting a plate that read "BG SUX" (former Bowling Green University grad student)...they didn't let me have it either. But when I moved to Sioux City, Iowa (abbreviation SUX), they DID let me have it.<P>So some of it depends on state. Man, those Ohio folks WERE tough.||||reg||10
